course: dictionary
lesson: 15623
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which meaning to use. The word ted is a good example. Look for clues such as a toy, a field, or a name.
explain: «Lily hugged her old ted before bed.» Here ted is a noun. Hugging and bed are the clues, so a ted is a cuddly toy bear.
explain: «The farmer had to ted the hay so it would dry in the sun.» Here ted is a verb. Farmer, hay and dry are the clues: to ted means to spread out cut grass or hay so it dries. Always test your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
explain: «Ted is coming to tea on Sunday.» Ted with a capital letter is a person's name, short for Edward or Theodore. The name is a clue in itself, so check the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Ted (noun, informal, UK and Australia) means a teddy bear.
fact: Ted (verb, farming) means to spread out cut grass or hay so it dries.
fact: A tedder is a machine that spreads hay.
fact: Ted is also a short form of the names Edward and Theodore.
fact: In history, a Teddy boy was a young man who wore a smart style of long jacket and narrow trousers.
exercise: «Lily hugged her old ted before bed.» What is a ted here? | A small lake | A young man in a long jacket | A machine that spreads hay | *A teddy bear
exercise: «The farmer will ted the grass in the morning so it dries.» What does ted mean here? | To hide in tall grass | *To spread out cut grass so it dries | To hug the grass | To cut the grass very short
exercise: «Ted is coming to tea on Sunday.» What kind of word is Ted here? | A teddy bear | A type of jacket | A verb about hay | *A name, short for Edward or Theodore
test: «My ted has one ear and a red bow.» What is my ted? | A machine that dries hay | *A cuddly toy bear | A farm worker who cuts grass | A Teddy boy from history
test: «The hay was tedded this morning and is ready to bale.» What does tedded mean? | *Spread out to dry | Cut into small pieces | Carried away on a truck | Covered with a tarpaulin
exam: Which sentence uses ted as a verb? | «My ted sleeps on my bed.» | «Ted went to the park with his dad.» | «Ted is my uncle's name.» | *«The farmer teds the hay so it can dry.»
